
err_method_type_param_uninferable.em:29  weird's own R cannot be worked out from this call.

   29 | print(b.weird([3, 4]).or(0))

  Two shapes say what R is: a trailing block whose own answer decides it, the way map's does, or an argument written as R itself, the way reduce(0) says Int. weird is neither — a R nested inside another type would have to be matched against the shape of what arrived, which is guessing rather than reading.

